# Did #482 regress 4K 8bpc? Settling the one cell the size sweep could not.

date: 2026-08-10
host: Apple M4 Pro (Mac16,11, 8P+4E, 24 GB), macOS 26.5.2 build 25F84
toolchain: rustc 1.97.1 (8bab26f4f 2026-07-14), default features, no `asm`,
      no `-C target-cpu=native`, no `nice` on any timed run
branch: verify/recheck-482-4k, base `main` @ 0f6bf10
write-up: docs/RECHECK_482_4K.md
issue: #455 (campaign index)

## arms

    parent   b0a00c3   #482's first parent on main
    head     2fae4fe   #482 as merged
    main     0f6bf10   current main
    headoff  2fae4fe   SAME BINARY as head, RAV1D_OWNED_RECON=0
    mainoff  0f6bf10   SAME BINARY as main, RAV1D_OWNED_RECON=0
    szrs     b0a00c3   the SIZE SWEEP's own staged binary, reused unmodified
    szrs2    2fae4fe   the SIZE SWEEP's own staged binary, reused unmodified

Binary provenance, checked before timing: `nm` counts 28 `owned_recon` symbols
in head, 16 in main, 0 in parent; the three binaries reproduce byte-for-byte
the sizes recorded in commit 2a7ff51's message (2,868,624 / 2,888,816 /
2,887,376). NOTE: 2a7ff51 (the 37 `#[inline]` -> `#[inline(always)]` seam fix)
is NOT in 2fae4fe -- it landed in the 2fae4fe..0f6bf10 range.

## vectors

Reused unchanged from the size-sweep ladder (`~/tmp/szsweep/vec`, 1.1 GB of
IVF kept out of git; recipe in `~/tmp/szsweep/enc.sh` + `mkivf.sh`) plus the
campaign's `v4k_8tile` (`~/tmp/rav1d-perf/vec`). `L3840x2160_444_8b` is
byte-identical to the campaign's `v4k_1tile` (md5 690b8601...).

## load

NOT idle. 140 of 140 main-sweep groups and 22 of 22 mirror groups carry
foreign load. Absolutes are inflated; paired within-round ratios are the claim.

